  "notes": "HABS drawing and text: the Bachman House (c.1825, near Madison IN), a German immigrant's tavern 'built into an embankment similar to many early Pennsylvania stone houses -- the principal floor on the upper level, with the lower floor facing out from the hillside'; two square stone pavilions under one wide roof with a central breezeway (the dogtrot plan); a massive stone end chimney"
